    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f572d97d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a yellow snake with its mouth open, appearing to bite or hold a green lizard. The text overlay reads, \"this is a snakes mouth it all makes fucking sense now.\" The scene is a literal depiction of a predator-prey interaction in nature. There is no toxicity present in this meme. The intent is to use the visual of the snake's mouth to create a humorous or ironic realization, likely implying that something previously confusing or illogical now makes sense in light of this visual. The meme relies on the juxtaposition of the image (snake mouth) with the text to create a punchline, without targeting any specific group or engaging in harmful, hateful, or abusive content. The language is vulgar but not directed at any protected characteristic or community, and the content is purely observational and humorous, rooted in biological reality.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22ecb1b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
