      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_12cee8dc",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "predator_prey_interaction",
      "label": "Predator-Prey Interaction",
      "description": "The concept of predator-prey interaction is a fundamental biological and ecological principle. The meme relies on the viewer understanding that the snake is a predator and the lizard is prey, which is a natural and observable phenomenon in the wild. This knowledge allows the viewer to interpret the image as a literal depiction of a hunting or feeding behavior, which is then humorously juxtaposed with the text overlay. Without this background knowledge, the visual might be misinterpreted as something else (e.g., a staged photo or a symbolic image), and the punchline of the meme would not make sense.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22ecb1b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0e038e1f",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "snake_mouth_analogy",
      "label": "Snake Mouth Analogy",
      "description": "The meme uses the visual of the snake's mouth to create an analogy or metaphor. The text 'this is a snakes mouth it all makes fucking sense now' implies that the viewer has just realized something previously confusing or illogical now makes sense — likely because it is literally a snake's mouth. This requires the viewer to understand that the image is not metaphorical but literal, and that the realization is based on a direct visual observation. The background knowledge here is the understanding that the image is a literal depiction of a biological fact, not a symbolic or abstract representation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22ecb1b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_42f89394",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "vulgar_language_use",
      "label": "Vulgar Language Use",
      "description": "The text overlay contains the phrase 'all makes fucking sense now', which uses vulgar language. The use of such language in memes is a cultural phenomenon that conveys a sense of exasperation, relief, or sudden realization. Understanding the context and tone of this language requires knowledge of internet culture and meme conventions, where swearing is often used to emphasize emotion or to add humor. This background knowledge helps the viewer interpret the tone of the meme — it is not meant to be taken literally as a threat or insult, but as an expression of humorous epiphany.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22ecb1b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c4da8a16",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "meme_format",
      "label": "Meme Format",
      "description": "The meme follows a common format: a visual image with text overlay that creates a punchline or realization. This format is a cultural phenomenon in internet communication, often used to express humor, irony, or sudden insight. The background knowledge here is the understanding that memes are a form of visual humor that relies on juxtaposition and context. Without this knowledge, the viewer might not recognize the meme as a joke or might misinterpret the intent of the text overlay.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22ecb1b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_608d88cc",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "sudden_realization",
      "label": "the sudden realization emotion",
      "description": "The emotion expressed is one of epiphany or 'aha' moment, where the viewer suddenly understands something previously confusing or illogical. This is conveyed through the text overlay 'this is a snakes mouth it all makes fucking sense now', which implies the viewer has just connected the visual with a prior mental puzzle. The emotion is humorous and relieved, as the realization resolves ambiguity.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22ecb1b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f0152c21",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "snake_mouth_realization_mapping",
      "label": "Text identifies the visual as a snake's mouth",
      "description": "The top text overlay 'this is a snakes mouth it' explicitly maps the visual entity 'yellow_snake' (specifically its open mouth) to the textual concept of 'a snake's mouth'. This is the core analogical mapping that enables the punchline 'all makes fucking sense now', as the viewer realizes the visual is literally a snake's mouth, resolving prior confusion. The mapping is direct and literal, based on the text's explicit identification of the visual element.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22ecb1b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_17e799f8",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual realization",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'all makes fucking sense now', as the meme implies the viewer is having a sudden, humorous epiphany. The text directly addresses the user's perspective, making them the subject of the realization.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22ecb1b5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1868a612",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "general internet audience",
      "description": "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience familiar with meme culture, visual humor, and vulgar language conventions. It relies on common internet meme formats (image + text punchline) and does not target any specific demographic, community, or protected group. The humor stems from a literal biological observation (snake mouth) and a sudden realization, which is accessible to anyone with basic understanding of predator-prey dynamics and internet humor norms. The use of vulgar language ('fucking') is a common trope in internet memes to convey exaggerated emotion or relief, not directed at any specific community.",
